%% Source for confirmed-write-light.svg and confirmed-write-dark.svg.
%%
%% The README shows those files as an <img> rather than a ```mermaid``` block.
%% GitHub renders Mermaid inside a viewer that floats pan, zoom and copy controls
%% over the corners of the drawing, and they sat on top of a node. An image
%% carries no such overlay. The cost is that the picture no longer regenerates
%% itself when this file changes — re-render both themes after editing:
%%
%%   python3 docs/img/render_sequence.py
%%
%% That script owns the palette, the two colour schemes and the pixel dimensions
%% an <img> needs. Do not call mermaid-cli directly: its defaults are a generic
%% blue-and-lilac that belongs to no product, and the width it emits is "100%%",
%% which an <img> cannot size itself from.

sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    %% Ordered as the chain actually runs, so every message is one hop and no
    %% arrow crosses a lifeline it has nothing to do with. The page sits between
    %% the agent and the gateway because that is now literally where it sits.
    actor W as Worker
    participant A as Voice Agent
    participant P as Page
    participant G as Gateway
    participant S as S/4HANA

    W->>A: "twenty pieces of 4711 arrived"
    Note over A: the agent has no write tool yet
    A->>P: prepare_goods_receipt(4711, 20)
    P->>G: /api/voice-tools/… + session capability
    G->>S: stock, description, bin
    S-->>G: 280 EA · hex bolt M8×40 · A-03-02
    G-->>P: prepared · one-use token · valid 2 min
    P-->>A: result — and now post_goods_receipt exists
    A-->>W: "Twenty pieces of hex bolt M8 by 40,<br/>into bin A-03-02. Confirm?"
    W->>A: "confirm"
    A->>P: post_goods_receipt(token + the spoken sentence)
    P->>G: /api/voice-tools/… + session capability
    G->>G: token unused? same intent in the last 120 s?
    G->>S: X-CSRF-Token: Fetch
    S-->>G: token
    G->>S: POST A_MaterialDocumentHeader · movement 501
    S-->>G: document 4900000123
    G-->>P: posted
    P-->>A: result
    A-->>W: "Posted. Material document 4900000123."
    G--)P: live screen updates over SSE
